WEBVTT

00:00:00.302 --> 00:00:02.912
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Do you speak English at work?

00:00:04.175 --> 00:00:08.951
<v><b>F:</b></v> What do these people have in common: a banker in Mexico City,

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:17.164
a barman in a five-star hotel in Warsaw, and a worker in the Hitachi electronics factory in Tokyo.

00:00:18.161 --> 00:00:20.654
They all speak English at work.

00:00:21.778 --> 00:00:24.033
Do you speak English at work?

00:00:24.403 --> 00:00:25.881
Write and tell us.

00:00:27.366 --> 00:00:28.270
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Marcos

00:00:29.903 --> 00:00:33.162
<v><b>Marcos:</b></v> I work in a restaurant in Madrid. I’m a waiter.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:39.141
I speak English at work every day, because a lot of tourists come here.

00:00:40.219 --> 00:00:45.189
I help customers with the menu and I say what the special dishes are.

00:00:46.255 --> 00:00:49.739
They are very happy because they can talk to me in English.

00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:55.606
A lot of tourists don’t speak Spanish, but they usually speak English.

00:00:57.627 --> 00:00:58.503
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Charlotte

00:00:59.938 --> 00:01:03.609
<v><b>Charlotte:</b></v> I’m a receptionist and I work in an office in Paris.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.030
It’s a multinational company.

00:01:07.043 --> 00:01:12.547
When people from other countries visit the company I need to welcome them in English.

00:01:13.325 --> 00:01:16.225
I also need to answer the phone in English.

00:01:17.117 --> 00:01:22.674
When we have meetings we all speak in English, because it’s the language of the company.